    "c2": {
      "anchor": "q2",
      "kind": "item",
      "label": "How should pages reach a place that needs a key: Spell's page server, or a place server of Jarvis's own?",
      "excerpt": "How should pages reach a place that needs a key: Spell's page server, or a place server of Jarvis's own?",
      "text": "what is this in reference to?",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-19T03:14:10.245Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-19T03:15:01.969Z",
          "html": "<p>It's from your third paste, about <code>JARVIS_TOKEN</code>. The Jarvis Jobs page can't read Jarvis in a browser, even with the token set, for two reasons:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>A Spell page won't hold a secret key.</li>\n<li>Spell's local page server doesn't pass a project's keyed places through the server side that does hold keys (<code>PlaceServer</code>).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Q2 asks which should fix that:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>A: Spell's page server learns to serve every project's keyed places.</li>\n<li>B: Jarvis runs its own small place server.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>It feeds the \"Keyed Places Served\" phase.</p>"
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  "on": {}
}
